Z||000000||KnightRyder31||04-25-2000||08:59 PM||||1st Question, how can I make my 84 fiero faster? It just has a 4cyl. I dont a too much cash.<BR>2nd and last Question, why does my check engine light come on? It only comes on for a couple mins, then turns off again.....what the heck? Someone told me it was the EGR. I dont know, help!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rodrv6||04-25-2000||09:45 PM||||There probably isn't much you can do to get more power out of the 4 cylinder that wouldn't involve rather large sums of money.  The most common way seems to be to add 2 more cylinders in the form of an engine swap to a V-6.<BR>As far as the light is concerned, When it comes on the engine computer stores a trouble code in its memory.  This code will stay in memory unless the battery is disconnected.  Your best bet would probably be to get a Haynes shop manual and follow the instructions in it to retrieve the code or codes and see what the problem is.  If you know someone who is familiar with General Motors cars they can probably help you.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||04-25-2000||09:51 PM||||Get the code from your ECM <A HREF="http://www.syty.org/d&e.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.syty.org/d&e.html</A>  This will tell you what is not running right, but not always what part. It's a start!||||reg||1
Z||000003||KnightRyder31||04-26-2000||11:14 AM||||Well, could I put ram air on the car? I have heard of people doing this before. I just dont want to spend anything over $500.00, that would be too excesive. I really like my cars looks, and dont want to buy any other car with a bigger engine. How much would it cost to add a V6? And is there any easy way of putting one in?<BR>Thanks<p>[This message has been edited by KnightRyder31 (edited 04-26-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000004||Standard||04-26-2000||02:15 PM||||well, it already has cold air induction from the factory, and ram air wouldn't do all too much for the duck.  All you have to do for ram air, tho, is buy on of Tom's scoops... <A HREF="http://tom.fieroproject.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://tom.fieroproject.com/</A> ||||reg||1
